MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_001: Hey, Loretta, you're a temple apprentice, right?\nIf you ever need anything, feel free to ask me.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_002: Urgh, quit hovering. You don't need to fuss over me\nlike that.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_003: Oh, but I do. I'm older than you, and I'm senior to\nyou in temple work.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_004: If you need any instruction, or if you're ever in\ntrouble, I'm here to help.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_005: Well, maybe I oughta be studying up for the priest\nlady's sake. But what's the use?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_006: Nice of you to offer, but I'll figure it out.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_007: Even if you did help me study, it wouldn't stick.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_008: If you're not good with classroom learning, let me\nshow you. If we do it together, you'll remember it.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_009: That's way too much hassle! Any problems I got,\nI'll deal with 'em myself.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_010: Besides, I'm just an apprentice. There's not too much\nI need to know just yet.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_011: You're a temple priest! You need to study for the\nsake of the god you serve!
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_012: Says you! I'm not like you, lady. I'm just gonna do my\nthing and whatever happens, happens.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_013: I don't know what gods need. Hell, I barely even\nbelieve in half this stuff.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_014: You know, to be honest, I'm the same way.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_015: Originally, I only got into temple service because of\nmy grandfather's debt.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_016: No kidding? But you seem so serious about\nserving Aurora.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_017: Well, she's such a lovely person. I just want to do\nwhatever I can for her.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_018: Yeah, that's not the vibe I get from Credna.\n"Lovely" is the last word I'd use.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_019: That's really not what I'm talking about. But I'm sure\nyou'll understand...someday.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_020: Which is why I think... Huh?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_021: Did you see that? Look over there.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_022: What are you talking about? I don't see anything.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_023: Gotcha! That'll teach you to let your guard down.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_024: What the hell?! Let go of my arm, you weirdo!
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_025: Hmhmhm, I'll have you know I looked after my\ntroublesome little brother and sister for years.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_026: So you might as well give in now and study with\nyour big sis.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_C_027: Nooo!
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_001: So, now do you understand how to store and handle\nthe temple's valuable tools and objects?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_002: Ughhh. I wanted some sword training, not this\npaper-pushing busywork.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_003: Enough with the mouth! Try using your brain!\nAre you even listening to me?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_004: You can tell if a scroll's an original from what the\naxle's made out of and the symbols carved in it.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_005: You said studying was hard for you because you\nnever remember anything. But that was perfect!
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_006: Yeah, 'cause you kept nagging me. I even remember\nhow to wrap the adamantine cup for rituals.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_007: And that method is...
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_008: "Use cheap millet straw paper carefully. If it's torn,\nrepair it before continuing."
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_009: Yes! Exactly! When Credna finds out how hard\nyou've been working, he'll be overjoyed!
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_010: Gotta say, I've been taking better care of his tools\nthan I used to.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_011: I caught myself thinking, "Credna deserves better\nthan doing things halfway."
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_012: Hehe. It's wonderful to hear you say that. You're\nlearning to keep the gods in your heart.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_013: Faith develops with little steps like this. But you're\nfiguring that out, huh?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_014: You might be right. Maybe I do got it in me to be\na decent priest.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_015: Of course you do! Try hard, and you'll be rewarded\nfor your effort. And everyone will be happy for you.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_016: Huh. I mean, you're doing pretty good for yourself\nas a priest. Your family cheering you on?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_017: Naturally. When I made attendant priest, they had\na three-day party! Hahaha.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_018: That good, huh? Maybe if I do good, Ozin'll be\nhappy with me too.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_019: He's been looking out for me ever since I started\nserving at the temple.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_020: He taught me how to use a sword. And whenever I\nmessed up, he let me have it.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_021: It's good for an orphan like me to have someone\nwho'll do that, since my parents aren't around.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_022: I agree! And won't he be pleased when he sees how\nsuccessful you are at your temple work?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_023: I'll do my absolute best to help you. Hey, wait there\nfor a moment.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_024: Here we go. Temple Historical Review, Reign of the\nGods... Some specially selected reading for you.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_025: These are way too advanced for me! I can't read\nthis stuff!
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_026: Oh yes you can! And if you need me to explain\nanything, just ask.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_027: Why do you get so worked up over helping me?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_028: Let's just say it comes from wanting to help family.\nLet me assist you, even when it's boring, OK?
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_029: And, Loretta, I'm really happy you made a good\nfriend in Ozin.
MID_SE_Hur_Lor_B_030: I got a good friend in you too, Ultand.